# Both spellings. With the trailing slash git matches a directory only, so a
# `node_modules` SYMLINK — which is how a worktree borrows one — is not ignored
# by the slashed pattern and rides into `git add -A`. The bare one catches it.
node_modules
node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.bak
.vite-remote/
.vite/
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Emitted by `tsc -b` beside the vite configs it typechecks. The build output
# that ships is `dist/`; these are incidental. They are worse than clutter in
# one specific case: vite prefers `vite.config.js` over `vite.config.ts`, so a
# stale copy silently becomes the config that `npm run dev` and
# `npm run build:spa` use while edits to the maintained .ts are ignored.
vite.config.js
vite.config.d.ts
vite.remote.config.js
vite.remote.config.d.ts
vitest.config.js
vitest.config.d.ts
